  "slug": "dynamics-somatic-l1-19d0",
  "summary": "Seven preprints apply k-mer, long-read and single-cell multimodal methods to resolve satellite, methylation, histone, folding and karyotype variation.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is measurement strategies that resolve variability bulk or assembly-based approaches average out. Assembly-independent k-mer tools size Yq12 arrays across 1,597 males, revealing population variation, father-son dynamics and testis-expressed satellite RNA. Epigenomic methods extend resolution: ChIMe-seq jointly profiles histone modifications, DNA methylation and nucleosome positioning in single molecules and cells; TrES-seq pairs scRNA-seq with nanobody-based histone mark profiling in human tonsil cells; COMET assigns bulk long-read reads to cell types by methylation, separating composition shifts from within-cell changes. Single-base 5mC/5hmC profiling reports a 5hmC-to-5mC transition at gene bodies during mouse ES neuronal differentiation. Two studies quantify variability directly: genome folding differs between pluripotent and hepatocyte-like cells, and acral melanomas show continuous karyotypic and structural fluctuation (25 to over 200 chromosomes per cell) linked to MMBIR repair. The systems are heterogeneous; the shared element is methodology, not mechanism.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-22"
}
